1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,070
ANDREW: Good morning, Clare House Hotel. Andrew speaking. I'm the Events Manager.

2
00:00:08,070 --> 00:00:11,456
SAM: Good morning, Andrew. My name's Samantha.

3
00:00:11,456 --> 00:00:16,292
I'm arranging a party for my parents' fiftieth wedding anniversary,

4
00:00:16,292 --> 00:00:22,580
and I'm ringing to ask about hiring a room some time next September.

5
00:00:22,580 --> 00:00:27,900
Also my parents and several of the guests will need accommodation.

6
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:32,300
ANDREW: OK, I'm sure we can help you with that

7
00:00:32,760 --> 00:00:36,220
Will you be having a sit-down meal or a buffet?

8
00:00:36,220 --> 00:00:39,420
SAM: Probably a sit-down.

9
00:00:39,420 --> 00:00:43,410
ANDREW: And do you know how many people there'll be?

10
00:00:43,410 --> 00:00:46,770
SAM: Around eighty, I think.

11
00:00:46,770 --> 00:00:53,770
ANDREW: Well we have two rooms that can hold that number. One is the Adelphi Room.

12
00:00:53,770 --> 00:01:00,770
That can seat eighty-five, or hold over a hundred if people are standing for a buffet.

13
00:01:00,770 --> 00:01:02,890
SAM: Right.

14
00:01:02,890 --> 00:01:04,760
ANDREW: If you have live music

15
00:01:05,460 --> 00:01:10,623
there's room for four or five musicians in the gallery overlooking the room.

16
00:01:10,623 --> 00:01:16,728
Our guests usually appreciate the fact that the music can be loud enough for dancing,

17
00:01:16,728 --> 00:01:19,170
but not too loud for conversation.

18
00:01:19,170 --> 00:01:24,000
SAM: Yes, I really don't like it when you can't talk.

19
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:29,734
ANDREW: Exactly. Now the Adelphi Room is at the back of the hotel,

20
00:01:29,734 --> 00:01:34,144
and there are French windows leading out onto the terrace.

21
00:01:34,144 --> 00:01:40,760
This has a beautiful display of pots of roses at that time of the year.

22
00:01:40,760 --> 00:01:43,700
SAM: Which direction does it face?

23
00:01:43,700 --> 00:01:51,410
ANDREW: Southwest, so that side of the hotel gets the sun in the afternoon and early evening.

24
00:01:51,410 --> 00:01:53,850
SAM: very nice.

25
00:01:53,850 --> 00:02:00,319
ANDREW: From the terrace you can see the area of trees within the grounds of the hotel,

26
00:02:00,319 --> 00:02:03,320
or you can stroll through there to the river

27
00:02:03,960 --> 00:02:08,310
that's on the far side, so it isn't visible from the hotel.

28
00:02:08,310 --> 00:02:10,660
SAM: OK.

29
00:02:10,660 --> 00:02:13,867
ANDREW: Then another option is the Carlton Room.

30
00:02:13,867 --> 00:02:19,760
This is a bit bigger. It can hold up to a hundred and ten people.

31
00:02:20,020 --> 00:02:22,686
and it has the advantage of a stage,

32
00:02:22,686 --> 00:02:25,940
which is useful if you have any entertainment

33
00:02:26,320 --> 00:02:29,500
or indeed a small band can fit onto it.

34
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:33,440
SAM: And can you go outside from the room?

35
00:02:33,440 --> 00:02:38,360
ANDREW: No, the Carlton Room is on the first floor

36
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:42,620
but on one side the windows look out onto the lake.

37
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:47,890
SAM: Lovely. I think either of those rooms would be suitable.

38
00:02:47,890 --> 00:02:52,770
ANDREW: Can I tell you about some of the options we offer in addition?

39
00:02:52,770 --> 00:02:55,000
SAM: Please do.

40
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:00,500
ANDREW: As well as a meal, you can have an MC, a Master of Ceremonies

41
00:03:00,660 --> 00:03:03,660
who'll be with you throughout the party.

42
00:03:03,660 --> 00:03:07,480
SAM: What exactly is the MC's function

43
00:03:08,280 --> 00:03:12,760
I suppose they make a speech during the meal if we need one, do they?

44
00:03:12,760 --> 00:03:18,340
ANDREW: That's right. All our MCs are trained as public speakers

45
00:03:18,520 --> 00:03:20,542
so they can easily get people's attention -

46
00:03:20,542 --> 00:03:23,700
many guests are glad to have someone

47
00:03:23,700 --> 00:03:27,026
who can make themselves heard above the chatter!

48
00:03:27,026 --> 00:03:30,680
And they're also your support - if anything goes wrong

49
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:35,240
the MC will deal with it, so you can relax.

50
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:40,680
SAM: Great! I'll need to ask you about food

51
00:03:41,020 --> 00:03:43,592
but something else that's important is accommodation.

52
00:03:43,592 --> 00:03:47,360
You obviously have rooms in the hotel

53
00:03:47,820 --> 00:03:53,510
but do you also have any other accommodation, like cabins for example?

54
00:03:53,510 --> 00:03:58,584
ANDREW: Yes, there are five in the grounds, all self-contained.

55
00:03:58,584 --> 00:04:02,720
They each sleep two to four people

56
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:07,210
and have their own living room, bathroom and small kitchen.

57
00:04:07,210 --> 00:04:11,060
SAM: That sounds perfect for what we'll need.

58
00:04:11,060 --> 00:04:14,594
SAM: Now you have various facilities, don't you?

59
00:04:14,594 --> 00:04:21,220
Are they all included in the price of hiring the room? The pool, for instance.

60
00:04:21,220 --> 00:04:25,480
ANDREW: Normally you'd be able to use it

61
00:04:25,580 --> 00:04:28,301
but it'll be closed throughout September for refurbishment.

62
00:04:28,301 --> 00:04:33,612
I'm afraid. The gym will be available, though, at no extra charge.

63
00:04:33,612 --> 00:04:38,480
That's open all day, from six in the morning until midnight.

64
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:41,010
SAM: Right.

65
00:04:41,010 --> 00:04:46,402
ANDREW: And the tennis courts, but there is a small additional payment for those.

66
00:04:46,402 --> 00:04:51,794
We have four courts, and it's worth booking in advance if you possibly can,

67
00:04:51,794 --> 00:04:56,030
as there can be quite a long waiting list for them.

68
00:04:56,030 --> 00:05:00,460
SAM: Right. Now could we discuss the food

69
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:04,680
This would be dinner, around seven o'clock...
